<!--
    AML endpoint table.

    This ships EMPTY on purpose. AML destinations are run by national
    emergency services, they change, and some of them only accept traffic
    from OS vendors they have an agreement with. Sending an emergency
    location to the wrong number helps nobody, so please only add entries
    you got from an official source (the national regulator, the PSAP
    operator, EENA's AML deployment list) and that you have permission to
    use.

    You can replace this table without touching the app:
      * drop a file at /product/etc/cipheraml/aml_endpoints.xml
        (cipher.aml.mk can do this for you, see the README), or
      * overlay this resource with an RRO.

    Format:

    <country name="..."          Free text, only used in logs.
             mcc="234,235"       Network MCCs this entry applies to.
             iso="gb"            Country ISO codes, used when the MCC is
                                 not known yet (limited service).
             confidence="90">    Optional, overrides config_amlConfidencePercent.

        <trigger number="999" /> Numbers that start AML. Leave out every
        <trigger number="112" /> trigger to start on any emergency number.

        <sms destination="999"   Where the SMS goes.
             type="text"         "text" (default) or "data".
             port="..."          Destination port, only for type="data".
             optional-fields="false"  Also send al= and toc= when they fit.
             partial-imei="false" />  Send only the TAC part of the IMEI.

        <https url="https://..." />  Annex B HTTPS endpoint. https only.
    </country>

    Example (not a real endpoint, do not uncomment as is):

    <country name="Example" mcc="001" iso="xx">
        <trigger number="112" />
        <sms destination="112" />
        <https url="https://aml.example.invalid/v1" />
    </country>
-->
<aml-endpoints version="1">
</aml-endpoints>
